<figure class="cache-figure" data-cache-lease>
 <p class="figure-title">An expired lease does not stop its former owner</p>
 <label><input type="checkbox" data-safe checked /> A checks ownership before filling and releasing</label>
 <div class="lease-workers"><div><b>Loader A · captured £12</b><span data-a>Not started</span></div><div><b>Loader B · later reads £15</b><span data-b>Not started</span></div></div>
 <div class="cache-copy-pair"><div class="cache-copy"><small>Current lease owner</small><strong data-owner>None</strong></div><div class="cache-copy"><small>Saved answer</small><strong data-cache>Empty</strong></div></div>
 <div class="cache-controls"><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next event</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>0 / 5</span></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>Step to B’s acquisition: both source operations are running. B always checks ownership. The source changes before B reads it; the experiment focuses on A finishing after its lease expires. One Redis primary, no failover. Ownership checks do not replace the invalidation protocol from the previous article.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import {leaseState} from '../../lib/caching/stampedes.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cache-lease]').forEach(root=>{let step=0;const safe=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-safe]')!;const set=(n:string,v:string)=>{root.querySelector(`[data-${n}]`)!.textContent=v;};const render=()=>{const s=leaseState(step,safe.checked);set('a',s.a);set('b',s.b);set('owner',s.owner);set('cache',s.cache===null?'Empty':`£${s.cache}`);set('step',`${step} / 5`);set('explanation',s.message);for(const actor of ['a','b'])root.querySelector(`[data-${actor}]`)!.classList.toggle('loading',s[actor].toLowerCase().includes('loading'));root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-back]')!.disabled=step===0;root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')!.disabled=step===5;};safe.onchange=render;root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')!.onclick=()=>{step++;render();};root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-back]')!.onclick=()=>{step--;render();};root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.onclick=()=>{step=0;render();};render();});
</script>
